WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.062 --> 00:00:05.684
"Did you hear the big news?"

2
00:00:05.685 --> 00:00:10.647
Flo asked Ally as they were refilling the salt and pepper shakers the next morning at the diner.

3
00:00:10.648 --> 00:00:15.393
Ally gulped. "Flo likes Ray," she thought.

4
00:00:15.394 --> 00:00:21.135
"So she must be talking about Ray's wife coming back. I'll just pretend I don't know."

5
00:00:21.136 --> 00:00:25.059
"Big news?" Ally repeated. "What is it?"

6
00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:35.482
"It's huge!" Flo said. "Local bird-watchers spotted a pair of Southwestern bearded whoopers in the desert."

7
00:00:35.483 --> 00:00:41.981
"Oh, that!" Ally was relieved. "Yes, I saw that in the newspaper.

8
00:00:41.982 --> 00:00:47.001
The whoopers are endangered, right? That's why everyone is so excited about them?"

9
00:00:47.002 --> 00:00:52.597
"Yes! People also love them because they have a unique way of flying.

10
00:00:52.598 --> 00:00:54.344
Here, I'll show you a video."

11
00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:59.396
Flo found a video of whoopers flying on her phone and handed the device to Ally.

12
00:00:59.397 --> 00:01:05.881
"Wow!" Ally said. "It looks like their wings are moving in circles."

13
00:01:05.882 --> 00:01:11.441
While Ally was watching the video, Phil sat down on a stool at the counter next to another customer.

14
00:01:11.442 --> 00:01:14.678
"What are you watching, Ally?" he asked.

15
00:01:14.679 --> 00:01:16.831
Ally showed Phil the video.

16
00:01:16.832 --> 00:01:19.646
"It looks like they're dancing," Phil said.

17
00:01:19.647 --> 00:01:24.285
"You're right, it does!" Ally handed back Flo's phone.

18
00:01:24.286 --> 00:01:27.177
"What can I get for you this morning, Phil?"

19
00:01:27.178 --> 00:01:30.556
"Two scrambled eggs and toast," Phil replied.

20
00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.822
"Eggs and toast, coming up!"

21
00:01:32.823 --> 00:01:38.334
Ally pocketed her order pad and then spread her arms out wide and started spinning them in circles.

22
00:01:38.335 --> 00:01:45.045
"Hey, look at me, I'm a whooper!" Ally laughed as she headed for the kitchen.

23
00:01:45.046 --> 00:01:51.682
But she was so busy "flying," she didn't notice Randy coming out of the kitchen with a tray of freshly baked cupcakes.

24
00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:55.826
Ally's spinning "bird" arms hit the tray and sent it flying.

25
00:01:55.827 --> 00:01:58.567
Ally was about to activate her levitating powers.

26
00:01:58.568 --> 00:02:03.881
But the tray seemed to hover in the air for a split second before the customer next to Phil grabbed it.

27
00:02:03.882 --> 00:02:06.474
The customer set it down on the counter.

28
00:02:06.475 --> 00:02:11.281
Ally blinked in surprise. "Was I just seeing things?" she thought.

29
00:02:11.282 --> 00:02:15.013
"Or did that tray freeze in midair?"

30
00:02:15.014 --> 00:02:21.004
She turned to the customer.

31
00:02:21.005 --> 00:02:24.017
"Thank you so much for catching the tray!"

32
00:02:24.018 --> 00:02:27.549
"Happy to help," the customer replied.

33
00:02:27.550 --> 00:02:33.438
"Those cupcakes look too delicious to let them get ruined."

34
00:02:33.439 --> 00:02:38.200
"Would you like one?" Ally asked. "On the house, of course."

35
00:02:38.201 --> 00:02:46.615
"No, thank you," the customer said. "But I would love to know where you got your necklace."

36
00:02:46.616 --> 00:02:50.070
"My necklace?" Ally looked down.

37
00:02:50.071 --> 00:02:55.490
"Uh-oh!" she thought. Her meld medallion had slipped out from under her T-shirt.

38
00:02:55.491 --> 00:03:01.396
Ally quickly tucked it away. "It's nothing, just a present from my parents. More coffee?"

39
00:03:01.397 --> 00:03:10.103
"It's such an unusual piece—you must have very interesting parents," the customer said.

40
00:03:10.104 --> 00:03:13.023
"Are they world travelers?"

41
00:03:13.024 --> 00:03:17.975
"Um . . ." Ally smiled. "You could say that."

42
00:03:17.976 --> 00:03:24.649
The customer smiled back and laid a fifty-dollar bill on the counter to pay for her food.

43
00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:28.481
Ally started to give her change when the customer waved her off.

44
00:03:28.482 --> 00:03:37.921
"Keep it," she said with a smile. "And watch out for falling trays of cupcakes!"

45
00:03:37.922 --> 00:03:43.628
"She was so nice, and generous too," Ally thought as the customer left the diner.

46
00:03:43.629 --> 00:03:52.121
"Silly me, I imagined that tray floating in the air!"

47
00:03:52.122 --> 00:03:56.353
That afternoon Mateo came into the diner with a tall woman.

48
00:03:56.354 --> 00:04:00.050
She was wearing a beautiful dress and high heels.

49
00:04:00.051 --> 00:04:03.312
She looked like someone out of a fashion magazine.

50
00:04:03.313 --> 00:04:07.614
"Ally, this is my mother, Dawn," Mateo said.

51
00:04:07.615 --> 00:04:14.000
"It's so nice to meet you, Ally," Dawn said. "Mateo has told me so much about you."

52
00:04:14.001 --> 00:04:20.859
"I hope he hasn't said too much!" Ally laughed nervously. "Where's Ray?"

53
00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.725
"He had an errand to run," Dawn said.

54
00:04:23.726 --> 00:04:29.318
"I was so excited for my mom to see the diner, we came straight here."

55
00:04:29.319 --> 00:04:37.711
Mateo gave Dawn a quick tour, pointing out all the changes in the decor and showing her the new menu.

56
00:04:37.712 --> 00:04:40.348
"And here's Gourmet Greta's review."

57
00:04:40.349 --> 00:04:47.656
Ally pointed out the framed copy of the review hanging on the wall. "Greta loves it here!"

58
00:04:47.657 --> 00:04:53.606
"That's nice." Dawn smiled, but Ally could see she was thinking about something else.

59
00:04:53.607 --> 00:05:02.383
After a quick scan of Dawn's thoughts, Ally realized Mateo's mom was thinking about the fancy city restaurants she'd gotten used to.

60
00:05:02.384 --> 00:05:05.123
Ray's Diner was nothing like them.

61
00:05:05.124 --> 00:05:12.166
Dawn turned back to Ally. "I'm happy my sewing room is being put to good use as a place for you to stay.

62
00:05:12.167 --> 00:05:14.826
For now, anyway."

63
00:05:14.827 --> 00:05:20.883
"'For now'?" Ally thought. She spun around so no one could see her worried expression.

64
00:05:20.884 --> 00:05:30.607
"Yikes, Dawn does want her sewing room back. I really hope I can get onboard that P.O.D.!"

